## Data Model

Three SQLite stores, all append-oriented.

**`traffic_audit.db` → `network_requests`**
`id`, `timestamp`, `source_ip`, `destination_url`, `method`, `headers_json`, `body_size`, `response_status`, `user_agent`, `referrer`, `origin_page`, `is_third_party`, `data_sent_categories`, `data_received_categories`

**`change_audit.db` → `file_changes`**
`id`, `timestamp`, `file_path`, `change_type`, `changed_by`, `old_hash`, `new_hash`, `diff_summary`, `reason_provided`, `approved_by`

Both are indexed on timestamp and on the primary lookup column. Query directly with any SQLite client.

